--TEST--
an `extend` block's body sees only what code outside its type sees: a `private` property and a `private` method of the extended class do not compile there, as anywhere outside the class — `rule:classes/an-extend-block-adds-members-to-a-type`
--FILE--
<?nvs
namespace App;

use Acme\Shop\Order;
use App\OrderTools;

autoload 'Acme\Shop' from './vendor/acme/shop/src';

extend Order as OrderTools {
    public function secretTotal(): int {
        return $this->secret;
    }

    public function secretCode(): string {
        return $this->code();
    }
}

echo (new Order())->secretTotal(), "\n";
// covers: lang:classes/extend-blocks
--FILE vendor/acme/shop/src/Order.nvs--
<?nvs
namespace Acme\Shop;

class Order
{
    private int $secret = 7;

    private function code(): string
    {
        return "x" . $this->secret;
    }
}
--FILE vendor/acme/shop/package.toml--
[package]
name = 'Acme\Shop'
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0471]: `Acme\Shop\Order::$secret` is `private`, so only `Acme\Shop\Order`'s own bodies reach it
%A
   |                ^^^^^^^^^^^^^ this access is inside `App\OrderTools`
%A
error[E0471]: `Acme\Shop\Order::code()` is `private`, so only `Acme\Shop\Order`'s own bodies reach it
%A
   |                       ^^^^ this access is inside `App\OrderTools`
%A
error: aborting due to 2 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
